# Shell scripts must keep LF line endings on every platform.
#
# core.autocrlf is true on the Windows machine this project is developed on, so
# without this rule a fresh checkout rewrites .sh files with CRLF endings. A
# CRLF shebang then fails with "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M", which is a
# confusing way to discover a line-ending problem. Forcing eol=lf for .sh keeps
# them runnable from Git Bash, macOS, Linux and CI alike.
#
# Everything else follows the local autocrlf setting, so Windows editors and
# tooling keep working normally.
*.sh text eol=lf
